Good news first: **your redeploy worked** — the new endpoint is live. I tested it and it correctly returns `401 Unauthorized: No token provided` (that's the auth wall doing its job, exactly as designed).

Now I just need to mint your API key, and there's one small thing only you can do, because it requires your logged-in session. Here it is — **the whole thing is one paste**:

## Do this (takes 20 seconds)

1. Go to **disciplinedos.com** and make sure you're logged in (refresh the page if it's been open a while).
2. Press **F12** → click the **Console** tab.
3. Copy-paste this whole block and hit **Enter**:

```javascript
(async () => {
  const db = await new Promise((res, rej) => {
    const r = indexedDB.open('firebaseLocalStorageDb');
    r.onsuccess = () => res(r.result);
    r.onerror = () => rej(r.error);
  });
  const tx = db.transaction('firebaseLocalStorage', 'readonly');
  const store = tx.objectStore('firebaseLocalStorage');
  const records = await new Promise((res, rej) => {
    const rq = store.getAll();
    rq.onsuccess = () => res(rq.result);
    rq.onerror = () => rej(rq.error);
  });
  let token = null;
  const now = Date.now();
  for (const rec of records) {
    for (const k of Object.keys(rec)) {
      const sts = rec[k] && rec[k].value && rec[k].value.stsTokenManager;
      if (!sts || !sts.accessToken) continue;
      token = sts.accessToken;
      if (sts.expirationTime > now) break;
    }
    if (token) break;
  }
  if (!token) { console.log('❌ Not logged in — sign in to disciplinedos.com first'); return; }
  const r = await fetch('/api/mcp/tokens', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + token },
    body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Hermes VPS' })
  });
  const data = await r.json();
  if (data.token) {
    console.log('✅ KEY: ' + data.token);
    prompt('Copy your API key:', data.token);
  } else {
    console.log('❌', JSON.stringify(data));
  }
})();
```

4. A little box will pop up with your key (`dos_mcp_...`). **Copy it and paste it back here.**

That's it. The moment I have that key, I'll wire Hermes, hand you the Claude Code + Codex configs, and run a live end-to-end test.

---

If the console feels too fiddly, the alternative is: re-launch Chrome with remote debugging + the Tailscale tunnel (like we did before), and I'll drive it and mint the key myself — no console needed. Just say the word and I'll walk you through the two commands.

That "core dump" is just the sandbox's node binary crashing on exit — both checks printed `✓` first, so the script is valid. The new version scans *every* Firebase storage location instead of guessing one.

Here's the updated snippet. **Clear the console, paste this, hit Enter:**

```javascript
(async () => {
  let token = null;
  try {
    const dbs = await new Promise((res) => {
      const r = indexedDB.open('firebaseLocalStorageDb');
      r.onsuccess = () => res(r.result);
      r.onerror = () => res(null);
    });
    if (dbs) {
      for (const sn of Array.from(dbs.objectStoreNames)) {
        const recs = await new Promise((res) => {
          const t = dbs.transaction(sn, 'readonly');
          const rq = t.objectStore(sn).getAll();
          rq.onsuccess = () => res(rq.result);
          rq.onerror = () => res([]);
        });
        for (const rec of recs) {
          const m = JSON.stringify(rec).match(/"accessToken":"(eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)"/);
          if (m) { token = m[1]; break; }
        }
        if (token) break;
      }
    }
  } catch (e) { console.log('IDB scan error:', e.message); }
  if (!token) {
    for (let i = 0; i < localStorage.length; i++) {
      const key = localStorage.key(i);
      if (key && key.indexOf('firebase:authUser') === 0) {
        const m = localStorage.getItem(key).match(/"accessToken":"(eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)"/);
        if (m) { token = m[1]; break; }
      }
    }
  }
  if (!token) { console.log('❌ No token. Firebase keys in localStorage:', Object.keys(localStorage).filter(k => k.includes('firebase'))); return; }
  const r = await fetch('/api/mcp/tokens', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + token },
    body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Hermes VPS' }),
  });
  const data = await r.json();
  if (data.token) { console.log('✅ KEY:\n' + data.token); prompt('Copy your API key:', data.token); }
  else { console.log('❌', JSON.stringify(data)); }
})();
```

This one:

1. Scans **all** IndexedDB object stores for the Firebase ID token (a JWT — the `eyJ...eyJ...` string).
2. Falls back to `localStorage` if IndexedDB comes up empty.
3. If it *still* finds nothing, it prints your actual Firebase storage keys so I can see exactly where it's hiding.

Paste it and send me whatever it prints — the `✅ KEY:` line, or the `❌` diagnostic line. Either way we'll have our answer.

